            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Kurt Gödel</strong><br>\nKurt Gödel was born on April 28, 1906, in Brno, which was then part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire. He was known to be a child prodigy, displaying an immense talent for mathematics and languages from an early age. His family called him \"Mr. Why\" due to his inquisitive nature. Gödel's interest in formal systems, which would later define his career, began to surface during his teenage years.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Academic Career</strong><br>\nGödel studied at the University of Vienna, where he was drawn to the works of philosopher and mathematician Gottlob Frege. After completing his doctoral dissertation in 1929, he became a part of the Vienna Circle, a group of philosophers and scientists. Despite his shy and introverted personality, Gödel's brilliance in logic and mathematics made him a prominent figure in academic circles.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Incompleteness Theorems</strong><br>\nIn 1931, Gödel published his incompleteness theorems, which have had a lasting impact on the philosophy of mathematics. These theorems showed that within any given branch of mathematics, there would always be some propositions that cannot be proven or disproven using the rules and axioms of that mathematical branch. This work challenged the previously held belief that all mathematical truths could be proven.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
